---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { getState, href } from '../../lib/data';
import { breadcrumbNode, pageGraph, webPageNode } from '../../lib/schema';

const title = 'Nevada HOA rules for an RV or boat | RV Storage Finder';
const description =
  'Nevada NRS 116.350, read November 19, 2026, allows reasonable limits on RV, watercraft, and trailer parking in a common-interest community. Not a right to store a rig at home.';
const path = '/rules/nevada/';
const checked = '2026-11-19';
const nevada = getState('nevada');
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { label: 'HOA rules', path: '/rules/' },
  { label: 'Nevada', path },
];
const schema = pageGraph([
  webPageNode({ title, description, path, dateModified: checked }),
  breadcrumbNode(crumbs),
]);
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} schema={schema}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>Nevada HOA rules for an RV or boat</h1>
    <p>
      This page quotes the Nevada Revised Statutes. It is not legal advice, not a ruling on your
      governing documents, and not a substitute for the city or county code.
    </p>
    <p>
      Checked <time datetime={checked}>November 19, 2026</time> on the
      <a href="https://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-116.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nevada Legislature’s copy of NRS Chapter 116</a>.
      NRS 116.350 is titled “Limitations regarding regulation of certain roads, streets, alleys or other
      thoroughfares; permissible regulation of parking or storage of certain vehicles.” The page read
      that day did not print an “Added to NRS” history line on this section. This page does not state
      an effective date.
    </p>
    <h2>Public roads, then the RV sentence</h2>
    <p>Subsection 1 says:</p>
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        In a common-interest community which is not gated or enclosed and the access to which is not
        restricted or controlled by a person or device, the executive board shall not and the governing
        documents must not provide for the regulation of any road, street, alley or other thoroughfare
        the right-of-way of which is accepted by the State or a local government for dedication as a
        road, street, alley or other thoroughfare for public use.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>Subsection 2 says:</p>
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        Except as otherwise provided in subsection 3, the provisions of subsection 1 do not preclude an
        association from adopting, and do not preclude the governing documents of an association from
        setting forth, rules that reasonably restrict the parking or storage of recreational vehicles,
        watercraft, trailers or commercial vehicles in the common-interest community to the extent
        authorized by law. The governing documents of an association may authorize the executive board
        of the association to impose a fine pursuant to NRS 116.31031 for any violation of the rules
        authorized pursuant to this subsection.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <h2>What those sentences do not decide</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Subsection 2 allows reasonable restrictions on recreational vehicles, watercraft, trailers, and
        commercial vehicles. It is not a right to keep one on a driveway or out of sight.
      </li>
      <li>
        Subsection 1 is about a public road in a community that is not gated and whose access is not
        controlled. It does not, by itself, stop a rule about a private driveway.
      </li>
      <li>
        Subsection 3 limits bans on certain utility-service, law-enforcement, and emergency-services
        vehicles. Those words are not “recreational vehicle” or “watercraft.”
      </li>
      <li>
        Chapter 116 is the common-interest community statute. This page does not read a community that
        sits outside that chapter, and it does not read a local ordinance.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Off-site storage is a different question</h2>
    <p>
      A facility listing in this directory is a storage lot, not a statement that an association allows
      the vehicle at the house. {nevada.cities.length} Nevada city pages list those lots.
    </p>
    <ul>
      {
        nevada.cities.map((city) => (
          <li>
            <a href={href(`/cities/${city.id}/`)}>
              {city.city}, {city.state_code}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
